  attribute DESIGN_WARNING of nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads : entity is
    "NOT A COMPLIANT 1149.1 DEVICE UNLESS SE = 1. There are no dedicated TAP pads on this " &
    "die: the TAP is muxed onto functional pads and does not exist while SE = 0 (see " &
    "COMPLIANCE_PATTERNS). HOSTIO4_P1_0 and HOSTIO4_P1_1 are declared here as scalar " &
    "ports but are bits 0 and 1 of the chip's HOSTIO4_P1 port -- a VHDL attribute cannot " &
    "name a bus element, so the TAP pins are split out. PIN_MAP binds them to the same " &
    "physical pins either way, and the remaining bits are NOT renumbered. The four TAP " &
    "pins (SWDCK, SWDIO, HOSTIO4_P1_0, HOSTIO4_P1_1) still carry boundary-scan cells, and " &
    "while SE = 1 the pad ring overrides those pads. EXTEST cannot independently drive " &
    "them; treat their nets as untestable from this die. SE is the compliance-enable pin " &
    "AND has a boundary-scan cell, which BSDL does not expect. Hold SE at its compliance " &
    "value throughout; never drive that cell. HIGHZ IS NOT IMPLEMENTED. 15 output pads " &
    "have no output-enable cell and no instruction can tri-state them. IDCODE DOES NOT " &
    "IDENTIFY A MANUFACTURER. SoC Labs holds no JEDEC JEP106 allocation, so the " &
    "manufacturer field is set to 0x000 -- a code JEP106 can never issue -- and the part " &
    "number field is 0x0001. Your tools will report the manufacturer as invalid or " &
    "unknown; that is correct and intended, not a fault. Do not identify this device by " &
    "its IDCODE. PIN NUMBERS ARE PLACEHOLDERS (TBD_*) and no power, ground or analog pins " &
    "are declared. This file is not yet fit for production board test.";

end nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads;
